/**
 * The bytes the builder emitted for every CCD and Referral Note conformance init
 * BEFORE this change, captured at commit `52d5922` (whose `src/` tree is
 * identical to spec pin `6a8c4f8`: the only delta between the two commits is two
 * `.github/workflows/` files). This is the AC-10 baseline for S0352-ccda-7, and it
 * exists because the referent of "byte-identical to what that init produced before
 * this change" stops being recoverable the moment anything under `src/builder/`
 * moves: a regression test written after that compares the change to itself.
 *
 * SYNTHETIC. Every document below is the emitted form of a
 * {@link BUILT_DOCUMENT_CASES} init, so it carries the same invented patient
 * ("Jane Q Doe") and the same prefixed, non-MRN-shaped identifiers declared in
 * `scripts/phi-allow-list.txt`. Nothing here was derived from a real document and
 * no real patient data appears in it.
 *
 * A `.ts` module rather than a directory of `.xml` files on purpose: this
 * repository tracks no XML document anywhere, and
 * `test/conformance/artifact-provenance.test.ts` asserts that over `git ls-files`.
 *
 * DO NOT REGENERATE. Regenerating this file from the current builder is the exact
 * failure mode it was committed to prevent. If a case's bytes have to change, the
 * change is a deliberate, reviewed move of the CCD or Referral Note emit surface,
 * and it belongs in a spec that says so.
 */

